entry-level jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wildfire kills 4 firefighters in Indonesia's Mount Bromo national park</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c934e198aa17963fe92627d98657f2b6c3ad66eae0f659983971f9967727da63</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291--7fc8c1dafd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest victims of Indonesia's wildfires were trapped by thick smoke and fast-spreading flames, authorities said. Meanwhile, the toxic haze from the fires has spread to Indonesia's neighbors.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP's Dipke detained amid call for fresh Delhi demo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d9729c7d181d1e267741340b564a019cc2734d9422e849cb157c5dd06bf602d</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849--c55ce4c4fba8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police placed the founder of the Cockroach Janta Party, Abhijeet Dipke, in preventive detention. He was calling for a protest in central Delhi in defiance of police efforts to restrict it.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hypersonic missiles highlight arms race on Korean Peninsula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bce76e670975f72d21d1b4859c5c3c852a82354c227b5187a99bb5b47c277e2d</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hypersonic-missiles-highlight-arms-race-on-korean-peninsula/a-79667084--2f8077093613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hypersonic-missiles-highlight-arms-race-on-korean-peninsula/a-79667084?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Both South and North Korea have tested weapons feared by military planners for their speed and ability to maneuver in flight.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>School roof collapse in Pakistan's Peshawar kills dozens of students and one teacher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:392ad5a7219c84f95fcb7944bff9e3a96044d8d35a17a238e4d65a325cbaef0e</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/school-roof-collapse-in-pakistan-s-peshawar-kills-dozens-of-students-and-one-teacher/a-79666091--1b9255d24f73.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/school-roof-collapse-in-pakistan-s-peshawar-kills-dozens-of-students-and-one-teacher/a-79666091?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Local authorities said more than 50 other people were injured in the disaster. Roof collapses have become increasingly common in Pakistan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Supreme Court hears Rahul Gandhi's Election Commission plea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68924f457ed255211d98708ea7798a23c97b59fe8baae1df15c09fa609e101d4</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-supreme-court-hears-rahul-gandhi-s-election-commission-plea/live-79665180--ca56cfca5fbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-supreme-court-hears-rahul-gandhi-s-election-commission-plea/live-79665180?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A petition filed by opposition leader Rahul Gandhi and others seeks an independent audit of India's sweeping voter deletions. Meanwhile, actor Imran Khan has reportedly been ordered to leave India.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea, China open border bridge after 12-year delay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53fc18c59c4f11ee4708426a577108ed09b099e9a65d2b1247dee58b9a7a7c2e</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-china-open-border-bridge-after-12-year-delay/a-79666112--b02034e8a849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-china-open-border-bridge-after-12-year-delay/a-79666112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Twelve years after it was constructed, the New Yalu River Bridge between China and North Korea is finally operational. It is the latest sign of warming ties between the two nations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea says it tested cruise missiles to be launched from sub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4b80e6b6b5299bc05e41482ea6a81177d2932afd687f238128b0f1259140207</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-says-it-tested-cruise-missiles-to-be-launched-from-sub/a-79664436--051a0d5a1bc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-says-it-tested-cruise-missiles-to-be-launched-from-sub/a-79664436?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean state media said the military test-fired cruise missiles designed to be launched from submarines. Pyongyang has ramped up weapons launches in recent weeks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:37:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
